1. Label a Node with Zone

	kubectl label node <node-name> zone=us-east-1a
	
	Example:

		kubectl label node worker-node-1 zone=us-east-1a

2. Verify the Label

		kubectl get nodes --show-labels

	Or filter specifically:

		kubectl get nodes -l zone=us-east-1a

	Or describe the node:

		kubectl describe node worker-node-1

3. Update an Existing Zone Label

		kubectl label node worker-node-1 zone=us-east-1b --overwrite

4. Remove the Zone Label

		kubectl label node worker-node-1 zone-

5. Label Multiple Nodes

		kubectl label node worker-node-1 worker-node-2 zone=us-east-1a



