Taints & Tolerations


Taints & Tolerations: → Isolate Nodes (Practical Notes)

This is how you reserve certain nodes (e.g., DB nodes, GPU nodes) so that only specific Pods can run there.

🔹 1. Core Idea (Very Important)
			Taint (on node) → “Don’t allow pods here”

			Toleration (on pod) → “I’m allowed to run here”

👉 Together = node isolation

2. Taint Syntax
	
	kubectl taint nodes <node-name> key=value:effect

Example: 

	# Verify node has the taint

	kubectl describe node ip-172-31-13-173 | grep -A5 Taints

	# Verify node has the label

	kubectl describe node ip-172-31-13-173 | grep -A10 Labels


	kubectl taint nodes ip-172-31-13-173 db=true:NoSchedule

	kubectl label nodes ip-172-31-13-173 workload=database


Effect							Meaning

NoSchedule					Pod won’t schedule

PreferNoSchedule		Avoid if possible

NoExecute						Evict existing pods




3. Practical Example (DB Node Isolation)

Step 1: Taint the Node

	kubectl taint nodes ip-172-31-13-173 db=true:NoSchedule

Now:

	No pod can run on worker-1

Try normal pod (will FAIL)

spec:

  containers:
    - name: nginx
      image: nginx

👉 Result:

Pod = Pending
Error: node has taint {db=true:NoSchedule}


Step 2: Add Toleration (Allow Pod)

spec:
  tolerations:
    - key: "db"
      operator: "Equal"
      value: "true"
      effect: "NoSchedule"

  containers:
    - name: postgres
      image: postgres

👉 Now:

	Pod can run on that node

4. Production Pattern (BEST PRACTICE)

	Only DB workloads run on DB nodes

Step 1: Label Node

	kubectl label nodes ip-172-31-13-173 workload=database

Step 2: Taint Node

	kubectl taint nodes ip-172-31-13-173 db=true:NoSchedule


Step 3: Pod Config (Both Required)

spec:
  affinity:
    nodeAffinity:
      requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
        nodeSelectorTerms:
          - matchExpressions:
              - key: workload
                operator: In
                values: ["database"]

  tolerations:
    - key: "db"
      operator: "Equal"
      value: "true"
      effect: "NoSchedule"


Result:

	Pod Type												Result

	DB Pod (with toleration)					Runs





Remove Taint (if needed)

		kubectl taint nodes ip-172-31-13-173 db=true:NoSchedule-




Common Mistakes:

	Only Taint (no toleration)

		→ Pod stuck in Pending

	Only Toleration (no affinity)

		→ Pod may run on any node


Always combine:

	nodeAffinity → select node

	toleration → allow access

